Applied to the javacc 7.0.13 output by //build-tools/bazel:javacc.bzl.

javacc reports end of input by throwing java.io.IOException out of FillBuff(), and
AstParserTokenManager swallows it at every catch site to produce the EOF token. Allocating that
exception is the largest single cost of parsing a short query, because fillInStackTrace() walks
AstParser's whole recursive-descent stack. Two changes here: the sentinel becomes one shared
instance, and FillBuff() latches end of input so that the probes readChar() makes past the end
stop calling read() on the stream it just closed -- a closed Reader answers with a freshly
allocated IOException of its own, which is the same cost coming back through the JDK. An
IOException from a genuine read failure is still the one the reader threw.

Regenerate this file whenever the javacc version pinned in MODULE.bazel changes: build
//jackson-jq-core:ast_parser_srcs, copy the generated SimpleCharStream.java into a/ and an edited
b/, and run `diff -U 5 --label a/SimpleCharStream.java --label b/SimpleCharStream.java`. The extra
context is not decoration: the ReInit() hunk is indistinguishable from the constructor above it
at the default of 3 lines.

--- a/SimpleCharStream.java
